WEBVTT

00:00:27.924 --> 00:00:31.691
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:31.724 --> 00:00:34.324
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:34.357 --> 00:00:36.257
Don't you think...

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.390
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.457
It's okay.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.958
I'll keep you safe.

00:00:46.058 --> 00:00:48.390
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:00:50.457 --> 00:00:53.557
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:00:53.591 --> 00:00:56.691
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:58.591
Mmm.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.123
Make than one minute.

00:01:49.657 --> 00:01:52.958
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.891
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.857
Do you smell something?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:26.991
Ann?

00:02:29.657 --> 00:02:31.190
Ann?!

00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:52.357

...3-4-2-0.

00:02:53.424 --> 00:02:55.490
All right. You're in there.

00:02:55.524 --> 00:02:56.624
Perfect.

00:02:56.657 --> 00:02:59.390
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:16.891 --> 00:03:19.924
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:19.958 --> 00:03:22.058
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:24.123 --> 00:03:26.757
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:28.724
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:28.757 --> 00:03:30.791
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:30.824 --> 00:03:32.457
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.891
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:36.223
Are we army rangers?

00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:38.924
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:40.024 --> 00:03:42.058
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:44.791
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.657
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:03:46.691 --> 00:03:48.424
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:03:48.457 --> 00:03:50.524
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:03:50.557 --> 00:03:52.591
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:52.624 --> 00:03:54.324
Nothing. What do you got?

00:03:54.357 --> 00:03:56.891
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:03:56.924 --> 00:03:59.991
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:04:00.024 --> 00:04:01.857
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:04:01.891 --> 00:04:03.657
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:04:03.691 --> 00:04:04.958
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:04:04.991 --> 00:04:06.958
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:06.991 --> 00:04:09.058
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.390
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:11.424 --> 00:04:12.457
What do you mean?

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.457
Look.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:14.657
Dad noted three murders

00:04:14.691 --> 00:04:16.591
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:19.157
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.958
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:22.991 --> 00:04:25.524
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:27.324
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:27.357 --> 00:04:28.891
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:28.924 --> 00:04:30.724
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:30.757 --> 00:04:32.757
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:32.791 --> 00:04:34.123
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:34.157 --> 00:04:36.357
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.624
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:38.657 --> 00:04:40.958
Yeah. Good.

00:04:40.991 --> 00:04:42.457
Dean...

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.924
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:45.624
I'm just kidding.

00:04:45.657 --> 00:04:48.490
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:06.857
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:06.891 --> 00:05:10.357
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:13.024
And last night, while you were...

00:05:13.058 --> 00:05:14.290
Out...

00:05:14.324 --> 00:05:15.624
Oh, good times.

00:05:15.657 --> 00:05:17.290
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:17.324 --> 00:05:18.924
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:18.958 --> 00:05:21.457
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.791
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:23.824 --> 00:05:25.390
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:27.591
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:27.624 --> 00:05:28.991
You said that.

00:05:29.024 --> 00:05:30.024
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:30.058 --> 00:05:32.058
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.390
Where's all their stuff?

00:06:02.424 --> 00:06:05.524
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:05.557 --> 00:06:08.190
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:08.223 --> 00:06:09.557
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:12.223 --> 00:06:15.090
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:15.123 --> 00:06:16.857
He's not a waiter.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.424
I'm sam connors.

00:06:23.457 --> 00:06:26.058
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.223
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:28.257 --> 00:06:30.190
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.624
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:32.657 --> 00:06:35.824
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:35.857 --> 00:06:38.757
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:38.791 --> 00:06:40.090
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:40.123 --> 00:06:42.290
You just need to take another look.

00:06:42.324 --> 00:06:43.724
Oh, finally.

00:06:46.257 --> 00:06:47.524
Cheers.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.791
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.691
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:19.324 --> 00:07:20.757
But you knew that.

00:07:20.791 --> 00:07:22.424
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:22.457 --> 00:07:24.257
Guilty.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.958
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:26.991 --> 00:07:28.924
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:31.524
I'm sam.

00:07:31.557 --> 00:07:35.991
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:36.024 --> 00:07:37.424
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:39.090
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:39.123 --> 00:07:41.657
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:41.691 --> 00:07:44.123
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:44.157 --> 00:07:46.490
Yeah, actually.

00:07:46.524 --> 00:07:49.357
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.557
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:07:51.591 --> 00:07:53.557
Selling their things this soon.

00:07:53.591 --> 00:07:55.691
But dad's right about one thing -

00:07:55.724 --> 00:07:57.958
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:07:57.991 --> 00:08:00.424
Even the rich ones.

00:08:03.223 --> 00:08:05.290
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:05.324 --> 00:08:09.123
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:09.157 --> 00:08:11.123
Why not?

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:12.724
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:12.757 --> 00:08:14.290
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:14.324 --> 00:08:16.324
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:16.357 --> 00:08:17.390
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:17.424 --> 00:08:20.290
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.457
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:32.357 --> 00:08:34.791
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:34.824 --> 00:08:36.157
Art history course.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.757
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:37.791 --> 00:08:39.591
It's like i don't even know you.

00:08:56.591 --> 00:08:57.691
Huh.Huh.

00:08:57.724 --> 00:08:59.891
And what was the providence?

00:08:59.924 --> 00:09:01.024
Provenance.

00:09:01.058 --> 00:09:02.490
It's a certificate of origin,

00:09:02.524 --> 00:09:03.857
Like a biography, you know?

00:09:03.891 --> 00:09:06.123
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:06.157 --> 00:09:07.857
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:07.891 --> 00:09:10.223
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:10.257 --> 00:09:11.691
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:11.724 --> 00:09:13.591
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:13.624 --> 00:09:15.024
Not me.

00:09:15.058 --> 00:09:16.424
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:16.457 --> 00:09:18.123
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.290
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:20.324 --> 00:09:23.624
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:23.657 --> 00:09:25.190
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:25.223 --> 00:09:27.724
Call sarah.

00:09:32.058 --> 00:09:33.490
Nice place.

00:09:33.524 --> 00:09:34.624
Yeah.

00:09:42.991 --> 00:09:44.090
Glad you called.

00:09:45.157 --> 00:09:47.324
Surprised, but glad.

00:09:47.357 --> 00:09:48.390
Yeah?

00:09:48.424 --> 00:09:50.223
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:09:50.257 --> 00:09:52.624
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:09:52.657 --> 00:09:54.724
Yeah.

00:09:54.757 --> 00:09:57.924
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:09:57.958 --> 00:09:59.390
Welcome to the club.

00:09:59.424 --> 00:10:01.857
You're kidding me.

00:10:01.891 --> 00:10:05.657
Man: here we are.

00:10:05.691 --> 00:10:07.290
The wine list.

00:10:20.691 --> 00:10:25.424
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:27.724 --> 00:10:28.757
And you?

00:10:28.791 --> 00:10:30.090
I will, too.

00:10:30.123 --> 00:10:31.157
Certainly.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.524
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:33.557 --> 00:10:34.591
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:34.624 --> 00:10:35.691
I was an artist -

00:10:35.724 --> 00:10:39.657
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:39.691 --> 00:10:41.657
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:41.691 --> 00:10:43.190
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:43.223 --> 00:10:44.290
Yeah.

00:10:44.324 --> 00:10:47.290
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:10:47.324 --> 00:10:51.024
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:10:51.058 --> 00:10:53.657
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:10:58.757 --> 00:11:01.058
So...what did you mean when you said

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.724
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:11:02.757 --> 00:11:04.490
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:11:04.524 --> 00:11:06.223
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:06.257 --> 00:11:09.390
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.490
It was my mom.

00:11:16.524 --> 00:11:18.757
She died about a year ago.

00:11:18.791 --> 00:11:21.357
Totally unexpected.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.824
It really threw me.

00:11:26.524 --> 00:11:32.190
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:32.223 --> 00:11:34.991
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:35.024 --> 00:11:38.624
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:38.657 --> 00:11:40.123
So...

00:11:45.257 --> 00:11:46.557
So, what about you?

00:11:46.591 --> 00:11:49.290
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:11:50.958 --> 00:11:52.691
Reasonably.

00:11:52.724 --> 00:11:55.891
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:12:04.123 --> 00:12:07.824
Another long story for another time.

00:12:13.991 --> 00:12:15.857
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:15.891 --> 00:12:17.058
Provenances.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:19.924
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:19.958 --> 00:12:22.257
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:23.757
And?

00:12:23.791 --> 00:12:27.024
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:27.058 --> 00:12:31.424
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:31.457 --> 00:12:33.457
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:35.991
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:36.024 --> 00:12:37.757
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:37.791 --> 00:12:39.624
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:39.657 --> 00:12:41.924
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:12:46.157 --> 00:12:47.958
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:12:47.991 --> 00:12:49.324
Painted 1910."

00:12:49.357 --> 00:12:51.424
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:12:55.724 --> 00:12:59.490
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:12:59.524 --> 00:13:01.724
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:05.791 --> 00:13:08.424
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:08.457 --> 00:13:10.958
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:10.991 --> 00:13:12.223
Then stored,

00:13:12.257 --> 00:13:14.591
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:14.624 --> 00:13:16.490
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:16.524 --> 00:13:19.190
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:19.223 --> 00:13:21.390
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:43.757 --> 00:13:45.324
Go ahead.

00:14:30.058 --> 00:14:31.424
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:31.457 --> 00:14:34.324
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:15:03.974 --> 00:15:06.240
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:06.974 --> 00:15:08.741
How's that my problem?

00:15:08.774 --> 00:15:12.108
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:12.141 --> 00:15:13.141
You're kidding, right?

00:15:13.174 --> 00:15:14.874
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:14.907 --> 00:15:16.974
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:17.007 --> 00:15:18.807
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:29.074 --> 00:15:31.141
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:32.907 --> 00:15:34.741
Hey, guys.

00:15:34.774 --> 00:15:37.041
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:37.074 --> 00:15:38.640
What are you doing here?

00:15:38.674 --> 00:15:40.874
Oh...

00:15:40.907 --> 00:15:42.240
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:42.273 --> 00:15:44.373
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:44.407 --> 00:15:46.208
What are you talking about, sam?

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.041
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:15:49.074 --> 00:15:50.607
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:54.041
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:15:54.074 --> 00:15:57.373
I always forget.

00:15:57.407 --> 00:15:59.474
There you go.

00:16:02.174 --> 00:16:03.974
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:16:04.007 --> 00:16:06.607
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:13.841 --> 00:16:15.741
So...

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:17.141
I had a good time last night.

00:16:17.174 --> 00:16:19.174
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:19.208 --> 00:16:22.174
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.741
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:26.774 --> 00:16:28.574
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:28.607 --> 00:16:30.841
We really are taking off today.

00:16:30.874 --> 00:16:33.041
Oh. Oh.

00:16:33.074 --> 00:16:34.474
Now that's too bad.

00:16:34.507 --> 00:16:37.307
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.741
The -

00:16:38.774 --> 00:16:40.373
That painting...

00:16:40.407 --> 00:16:42.607
Looks so good.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.941
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:16:45.974 --> 00:16:47.707
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:16:47.741 --> 00:16:49.741
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:16:49.774 --> 00:16:51.974
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:16:52.007 --> 00:16:53.440
We sold it to the telescas

00:16:53.474 --> 00:16:55.440
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:16:55.474 --> 00:16:57.974
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:16:58.007 --> 00:17:00.907
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:17:00.941 --> 00:17:02.874
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:17:02.907 --> 00:17:04.674
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:17:04.707 --> 00:17:06.307
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.407
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:10.273
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:10.307 --> 00:17:12.874
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:12.907 --> 00:17:14.440
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:14.474 --> 00:17:16.007
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:16.041 --> 00:17:18.373
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:18.407 --> 00:17:21.874
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:23.874 --> 00:17:25.741
Okay.

00:17:27.841 --> 00:17:30.841
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:30.874 --> 00:17:32.941
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:32.974 --> 00:17:36.907
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:36.941 --> 00:17:38.041
Any ideas?

00:17:38.074 --> 00:17:39.307
Okay, all right.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:41.807
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:41.841 --> 00:17:43.574
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:43.607 --> 00:17:45.373
Yeah? All right.

00:17:45.407 --> 00:17:47.874
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:17:47.907 --> 00:17:50.640
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:17:50.674 --> 00:17:52.774
What were their names again?

00:17:53.807 --> 00:17:55.108
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:17:55.141 --> 00:17:56.907
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:56.941 --> 00:18:00.407
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:02.440
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:18:02.474 --> 00:18:05.407
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:06.774
Well...

00:18:10.373 --> 00:18:12.307
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:13.907
The whole family was killed?

00:18:13.941 --> 00:18:16.674
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:16.707 --> 00:18:18.707
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:18.741 --> 00:18:22.507
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.307
Why'd he do it?

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.607
Well, let's look.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.640
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:28.674 --> 00:18:30.607
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.307
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:37.108
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:37.141 --> 00:18:39.574
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:39.607 --> 00:18:43.474
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:43.507 --> 00:18:46.607
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:47.607
Kkkch!

00:18:49.874 --> 00:18:51.807
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:18:51.841 --> 00:18:53.307
They were all cremated.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.041
Anything else? Yeah.

00:18:58.074 --> 00:19:00.974
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:19:01.007 --> 00:19:02.774
It's right here somewhere.

00:19:02.807 --> 00:19:04.707
Right. Here it is.

00:19:12.807 --> 00:19:15.440
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:15.474 --> 00:19:17.307
Sure.

00:19:21.407 --> 00:19:22.607
Dad...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.807
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:25.841 --> 00:19:27.674
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:27.707 --> 00:19:29.208
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:32.774
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:32.807 --> 00:19:35.574
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.240
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:42.273 --> 00:19:44.774
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:44.807 --> 00:19:46.607
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:47.974
The painting has changed, dean.

00:19:48.007 --> 00:19:50.307
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.974
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:19:52.007 --> 00:19:54.540
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:19:54.574 --> 00:19:56.574
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:19:56.607 --> 00:19:58.407
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:19:58.440 --> 00:19:59.774
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:19:59.807 --> 00:20:01.874
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:20:01.907 --> 00:20:03.273
It could give us some clues.

00:20:03.307 --> 00:20:04.574
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.674
I don't know.

00:20:06.707 --> 00:20:09.273
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:09.307 --> 00:20:11.373
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:11.407 --> 00:20:13.440
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:13.474 --> 00:20:14.707
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:14.741 --> 00:20:16.974
Dude...enough already.

00:20:17.007 --> 00:20:19.007
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:19.041 --> 00:20:21.108
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:21.141 --> 00:20:22.340
Just back off, all right?

00:20:22.373 --> 00:20:23.741
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:23.774 --> 00:20:25.440
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:25.474 --> 00:20:27.007
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:27.041 --> 00:20:28.108
What's the point, dean?

00:20:28.141 --> 00:20:29.607
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:31.373
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:31.407 --> 00:20:33.307
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.208
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.340
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:43.373 --> 00:20:46.340
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:20:48.741 --> 00:20:52.108
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:20:52.141 --> 00:20:54.074
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:20:55.074 --> 00:20:59.874
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:20:59.907 --> 00:21:01.774
But...

00:21:01.807 --> 00:21:03.807
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:06.108 --> 00:21:09.141
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:09.174 --> 00:21:10.373
Wouldn't she?

00:21:15.041 --> 00:21:16.807
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:21.807 --> 00:21:27.240
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:27.273 --> 00:21:28.640
But not the main part.

00:21:28.674 --> 00:21:30.574
What's it about?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:36.707
Yeah, all right.

00:21:36.741 --> 00:21:39.707
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:39.741 --> 00:21:43.108
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.074
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:21:57.108 --> 00:21:58.941
Hey, hi.

00:21:58.974 --> 00:22:01.208
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:03.974
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:22:04.007 --> 00:22:06.507
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:08.340
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:08.373 --> 00:22:10.440
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:10.474 --> 00:22:12.273
And look at the painting again.

00:22:12.307 --> 00:22:14.974
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:15.007 --> 00:22:16.174
Wait, what?

00:22:16.208 --> 00:22:19.307
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:21.841
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:06.974 --> 00:23:08.108
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:10.240
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:13.774 --> 00:23:15.008
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:15.041 --> 00:23:17.574
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:17.607 --> 00:23:21.474
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:21.507 --> 00:23:24.041
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:24.074 --> 00:23:25.374
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:25.407 --> 00:23:27.841
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:27.874 --> 00:23:29.240
Ugh.

00:23:29.273 --> 00:23:30.741
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:30.774 --> 00:23:31.807
Evelyn?

00:23:31.841 --> 00:23:33.407
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:38.307 --> 00:23:39.540
Evelyn?

00:23:50.074 --> 00:23:52.741
Evelyn?

00:23:52.774 --> 00:23:54.140
It's sarah blake.

00:23:54.173 --> 00:23:55.607
Are you all right?

00:23:55.641 --> 00:23:56.907
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:24:03.008 --> 00:24:05.707
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:15.108 --> 00:24:17.874
Hey. You all right?

00:24:17.907 --> 00:24:19.307
No, actually.

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:22.641
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:22.674 --> 00:24:25.108
And found her like that.

00:24:25.140 --> 00:24:26.273
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:26.307 --> 00:24:27.674
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:27.707 --> 00:24:29.540
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:29.574 --> 00:24:31.041
Who's killing these people?

00:24:35.173 --> 00:24:36.741
"What."

00:24:36.774 --> 00:24:38.207
What?

00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:39.474
It's not "who."

00:24:39.507 --> 00:24:42.407
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:47.907
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:24:47.941 --> 00:24:50.741
No.

00:24:50.774 --> 00:24:53.440
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:24:53.474 --> 00:24:54.807
It's impossible.

00:24:54.841 --> 00:24:56.507
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:24:56.540 --> 00:24:59.774
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:24:59.807 --> 00:25:02.041
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:07.941
You're joking.

00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:14.741
You're not joking.

00:25:14.774 --> 00:25:17.207
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:18.874
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:18.907 --> 00:25:22.574
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:22.607 --> 00:25:24.207
And there have been others before that.

00:25:24.240 --> 00:25:25.774
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:25.807 --> 00:25:28.173
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:28.207 --> 00:25:29.607
And that's the truth.

00:25:29.641 --> 00:25:34.507
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:35.540
I'm coming with you.

00:25:35.574 --> 00:25:36.941
What? No.

00:25:36.974 --> 00:25:39.407
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:39.440 --> 00:25:42.108
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:44.008 --> 00:25:46.008
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:25:46.041 --> 00:25:47.907
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:25:47.941 --> 00:25:49.474
But if you're right about this,

00:25:49.507 --> 00:25:51.507
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:25:51.540 --> 00:25:53.540
We might have got these people killed.

00:25:53.574 --> 00:25:56.540
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:25:56.574 --> 00:25:58.741
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:26:01.607 --> 00:26:03.474
So are we going or what?

00:26:03.507 --> 00:26:04.674
Sam

00:26:06.707 --> 00:26:08.041
Marry that girl.

00:26:11.041 --> 00:26:14.874
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:14.907 --> 00:26:17.474
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:36.607 --> 00:26:40.207
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:40.240 --> 00:26:42.407
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:43.874
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:26:48.907 --> 00:26:51.140
Sam, check it out.

00:26:51.173 --> 00:26:52.607
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:26:52.641 --> 00:26:54.607
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:26:54.641 --> 00:26:56.374
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:26:56.407 --> 00:26:59.140
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:26:59.173 --> 00:27:03.374
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:08.108 --> 00:27:10.774
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:21.574 --> 00:27:22.807
"Merchant."

00:27:31.540 --> 00:27:34.207
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:34.240 --> 00:27:37.474
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:37.507 --> 00:27:40.440
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:40.474 --> 00:27:43.008
Not exactly.

00:27:43.041 --> 00:27:45.474
We don't get paid.

00:27:45.507 --> 00:27:48.074
Well, mazel tov.

00:27:49.674 --> 00:27:51.807
Over there.

00:28:26.707 --> 00:28:30.874
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:30.907 --> 00:28:33.741
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:33.774 --> 00:28:34.974
Whenever a child died,

00:28:35.008 --> 00:28:37.240
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:37.273 --> 00:28:40.074
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:28:45.707 --> 00:28:47.474
Notice anything strange here?

00:28:47.507 --> 00:28:48.974
Uh, where do i start?

00:28:49.008 --> 00:28:50.540
No, that's not what i mean.

00:28:50.574 --> 00:28:51.641
Look at the urns.

00:28:53.907 --> 00:28:55.841
Yeah, there are only four.

00:28:55.874 --> 00:28:58.074
Mom and the three kids.

00:28:58.108 --> 00:28:59.807
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:29:02.074 --> 00:29:03.574
So where is he?

00:29:03.607 --> 00:29:06.207
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:08.074
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:08.108 --> 00:29:10.674
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:10.707 --> 00:29:12.307
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:12.340 --> 00:29:16.741
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:18.941 --> 00:29:22.240
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:22.273 --> 00:29:24.074
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:26.140 --> 00:29:27.440
Do you mind if i -

00:29:27.474 --> 00:29:29.841
No. Okay.

00:29:29.874 --> 00:29:31.841
Okay, i got it.

00:29:31.874 --> 00:29:32.941
Make a wish.

00:29:41.173 --> 00:29:42.574
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:42.607 --> 00:29:45.240
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:29:45.273 --> 00:29:49.941
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:29:49.974 --> 00:29:53.974
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:29:54.008 --> 00:29:56.041
You're not delusional.

00:29:56.074 --> 00:29:59.140
But there's a "but" coming.

00:29:59.173 --> 00:30:02.240
But...

00:30:02.273 --> 00:30:04.841
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:06.907 --> 00:30:08.041
Can i ask why?

00:30:10.108 --> 00:30:11.273
'Cause i like you.

00:30:13.674 --> 00:30:15.674
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:18.074 --> 00:30:20.807
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:20.841 --> 00:30:25.307
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:25.340 --> 00:30:27.074
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:27.108 --> 00:30:28.140
What do you mean?

00:30:28.173 --> 00:30:31.407
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:34.474
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:39.941 --> 00:30:43.240
Sarah...

00:30:43.273 --> 00:30:45.240
I had a girlfriend.

00:30:46.641 --> 00:30:49.041
And she died.

00:30:49.074 --> 00:30:52.807
And my mom died, too.

00:30:52.841 --> 00:30:56.841
I don't know, it's like...

00:30:56.874 --> 00:31:00.074
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:31:00.108 --> 00:31:01.707
Like death just follows me around.

00:31:01.741 --> 00:31:04.273
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:31:04.307 --> 00:31:06.774
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:06.807 --> 00:31:08.674
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:10.574 --> 00:31:15.474
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:15.507 --> 00:31:17.008
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:19.474
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:19.507 --> 00:31:21.807
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:21.841 --> 00:31:23.540
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:23.574 --> 00:31:24.707
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:24.741 --> 00:31:25.907
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:25.941 --> 00:31:27.974
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:28.008 --> 00:31:29.108
That's what life is.

00:31:30.173 --> 00:31:33.540
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:33.574 --> 00:31:38.108
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:38.140 --> 00:31:40.807
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:40.841 --> 00:31:43.041
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:43.074 --> 00:31:46.641
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:31:46.674 --> 00:31:51.207
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:31:55.240 --> 00:31:56.874
Am i interrupting something?

00:31:56.907 --> 00:31:58.707
No. Not at all.

00:31:58.741 --> 00:32:00.108
Apparently.

00:32:00.140 --> 00:32:01.941
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:32:01.974 --> 00:32:05.374
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:05.407 --> 00:32:07.907
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:07.941 --> 00:32:10.273
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:10.307 --> 00:32:12.374
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:12.407 --> 00:32:13.807
Economy-Style.

00:32:13.841 --> 00:32:16.074
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:16.108 --> 00:32:17.540
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:17.574 --> 00:32:19.974
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:33.641 --> 00:32:35.574
You guys seem to be

00:32:35.607 --> 00:32:37.707
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:37.741 --> 00:32:42.240
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:42.273 --> 00:32:46.574
Still think i'm a catch?

00:32:48.008 --> 00:32:50.074
Think i got something.

00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:17.974
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:20.008 --> 00:33:21.641
Good riddance.

00:33:33.140 --> 00:33:34.874
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:34.907 --> 00:33:37.707
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:37.741 --> 00:33:40.507
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:40.540 --> 00:33:41.641
I want to come with you.

00:33:41.674 --> 00:33:43.273
Are you sure?

00:33:43.307 --> 00:33:45.008
Hey, hey, hey.

00:33:45.041 --> 00:33:47.607
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:33:47.641 --> 00:33:49.474
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:16.874 --> 00:34:19.173
Uh, sam...

00:34:19.207 --> 00:34:21.941
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:21.974 --> 00:34:23.374
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:25.907 --> 00:34:28.008
Where's the little girl?

00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:31.974
And the razor?

00:34:46.941 --> 00:34:49.641
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:34:49.674 --> 00:34:51.140
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:34:56.340 --> 00:34:57.941
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:34:57.974 --> 00:34:59.674
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:34:59.707 --> 00:35:01.774
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:35:01.807 --> 00:35:03.307
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:35:03.340 --> 00:35:04.674
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:35:04.707 --> 00:35:06.140
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:06.173 --> 00:35:08.574
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:08.607 --> 00:35:11.407
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:11.440 --> 00:35:14.407
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:16.574
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:16.607 --> 00:35:18.574
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:21.707 --> 00:35:23.907
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:23.941 --> 00:35:26.407
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:28.307
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:28.340 --> 00:35:30.574
Hurry.

00:35:30.607 --> 00:35:34.173
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:34.207 --> 00:35:36.707
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:35:55.574 --> 00:35:56.674
Sam!

00:36:14.574 --> 00:36:16.874
That is just so wrong.

00:36:38.273 --> 00:36:41.108
Iron?

00:36:41.140 --> 00:36:42.173
Yeah.

00:36:42.207 --> 00:36:44.540
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:44.574 --> 00:36:45.574
Yeah, for now.

00:36:45.607 --> 00:36:46.974
How we gonna waste her?

00:36:47.008 --> 00:36:48.774
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:36:48.807 --> 00:36:51.041
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:36:51.074 --> 00:36:52.440
There must be something else.

00:36:53.741 --> 00:36:55.240
Sam, wait.

00:36:55.273 --> 00:36:57.440
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:36:57.474 --> 00:37:00.540
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:37:00.574 --> 00:37:03.707
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:37:03.741 --> 00:37:04.941
I mean, everything.

00:37:04.974 --> 00:37:07.407
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:07.440 --> 00:37:08.607
Dean?

00:37:08.641 --> 00:37:11.574
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:11.607 --> 00:37:14.574
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:14.607 --> 00:37:16.440
Both: the mausoleum.

00:37:45.207 --> 00:37:46.974
Sam!

00:38:11.974 --> 00:38:12.974
Come on, dean.

00:38:33.207 --> 00:38:35.140
Come on! Come on!

00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:28.474
Sam, you good?

00:39:32.607 --> 00:39:33.674
Not bad.

00:39:52.524 --> 00:39:54.958
This was archived in the county records.

00:39:54.991 --> 00:39:57.524
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:39:57.557 --> 00:39:59.123
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:39:59.157 --> 00:40:02.024
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:40:02.058 --> 00:40:03.290
She killed them?

00:40:03.324 --> 00:40:05.058
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:05.090 --> 00:40:07.290
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:07.324 --> 00:40:08.791
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:08.824 --> 00:40:11.024
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:11.058 --> 00:40:12.724
Where's this one go?

00:40:12.757 --> 00:40:14.357
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:16.290 --> 00:40:19.757
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:24.624
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:24.657 --> 00:40:26.624
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:26.657 --> 00:40:28.691
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:28.724 --> 00:40:31.390
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:31.424 --> 00:40:33.657
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:33.691 --> 00:40:36.324
We move on.

00:40:38.157 --> 00:40:39.757
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:40:46.524 --> 00:40:50.457
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:40:54.757 --> 00:40:56.924
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:40:56.958 --> 00:40:58.157
But don't thank me or anything.

00:41:04.190 --> 00:41:07.524
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:07.557 --> 00:41:10.457
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:10.490 --> 00:41:13.390
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:13.424 --> 00:41:15.924
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:15.958 --> 00:41:16.958
What's that?

00:41:16.991 --> 00:41:19.591
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:20.691 --> 00:41:22.290
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:22.324 --> 00:41:24.324
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:24.357 --> 00:41:27.724
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:27.757 --> 00:41:30.223
Maybe...

00:41:33.557 --> 00:41:36.024
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:39.691 --> 00:41:41.257
I will.

00:42:25.058 --> 00:42:27.691
That's my boy.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
